  "description": "A thread-safe, async object pool for expensive-to-create, reusable instances such as SMTP and database connections, network clients, and sockets. Hands items out under a lease and reclaims them on release, caps total instances with MaxSize (which doubles as a concurrency throttle), lazily evicts idle items, and runs an async readiness and preparation check before reuse. Includes dependency injection extensions, named pools, and System.Diagnostics.Metrics instrumentation. Targets .NET 10.",
